{"replacement":"function summarize(items, config) {
  const active = items.filter(item => !item.cancelled);
  if (active.length === 0) {
    return { subtotal: 0, discount: 0, shipping: 0, total: 0 };
  }

  const subtotal = active.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.cents * item.qty, 0);
  const discount = Math.floor(subtotal * config.discountBps / 10000);
  const net = subtotal - discount;
  const shipping = net >= config.freeShippingAt ? 0 : config.shippingCents;

  return { subtotal, discount, shipping, total: net + shipping };
}","explanation":"The implementation currently includes cancelled rows, rounds rather than floors the discount, always charges shipping, computes total before subtracting the discount, and returns nonzero results for an empty invoice. This replacement filters cancelled rows without modifying the supplied array or row objects, then applies the contract’s subtotal, floor-based discount, net, and free-shipping threshold using the supplied config values. When no active rows remain—including an empty list or a list containing only cancelled rows—it returns zero for all four fields. It assumes rows and config contain the fields described by the contract."}
